Workstream ID: keep-going-journal-research
Title: Research a journal-first Keep Going experience
Status: DONE
Milestone: Deliver an evidence-informed, section-scoped design direction
Dependencies: None
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/CareerOS/issues/21
Purpose: Research how a retrospective personal journal could support voluntary
  reflection on actual recorded work. Compare psychology evidence and its
  limits, then propose a newest-first, journal/moodboard direction for Keep
  Going only. This is research and design rationale, not website implementation.
  Keep the private design brief and supplied references out of public tracking.

Tasks:
  [x] Read the current section, record models, date semantics and privacy contract.
  [x] Review primary psychology and relevant interface/accessibility evidence.
  [x] Include mixed findings and separate theory from tested interventions.
  [x] Compare visual alternatives without claiming a layout has proven benefits.
  [x] Specify honest reverse chronology, record provenance and empty states.
  [x] Distinguish presentation-only ideas from new media or persistence features.
  [x] Deliver a detailed source-linked private brief and compact recommendation.
  [x] Record scope, limitations and verified same-identity tracking.

Acceptance criteria:
  Findings identify actual sources, reviewed scope and important limitations.
    No medical, mood-improvement or learning-outcome guarantee is made.
  Design consequences are explicitly proposals, not validated product outcomes.
    Keep the recommendation bounded to the existing Keep Going section.
  Newest-first order respects supplied event dates versus saved-record dates.
    Unknown dates and sample/tutorial provenance are not silently invented.
  Preserve readable typography, canonical themes, meaningful source details and
    keyboard/mobile access. Distinguish logical order from collage decoration.
  Actual history, private input, reference images and report bodies stay out of
    issues, shared continuity and public repository documents.
  Do not inspect browser data, change the app/schema, fabricate accomplishments,
    implement deferred features, stage, commit, push or deploy.
  Human design acceptance and any later implementation remain separate.

